# Phase 4 — "leave it running". Written 2026-08-27 for the first unattended run.
#
# Parked on 466.0 rather than rotating. Phase 4 is a stability and threshold
# gate, and the band-switching trap in docs/bench-bringup.md is documented but
# unverified — a retune that carries noise-floor state across bands produces a
# burst of false detections after every switch. That is a variable worth adding
# only when somebody is watching. 466 is also the band the survey exists for.
#
# 2.5 MSPS, not 10, and this was changed after measuring it. The first start of
# this run at 10 MSPS held 109-114 fps against a target of 153 — 26% short, with
# overflows climbing continuously against 7080 events/hour of real Boston
# traffic. Overflows are dropped samples, and dropped samples corrupt level and
# duration, which are the two things an airtime survey exists to measure. Three
# weeks of 26%-lossy data over 10 MHz is worth less than three weeks of clean
# data over 2.5, so the span goes and the integrity stays.
#
# It also means the question this run was partly meant to answer — what IS the
# overflow rate under real diurnal load — got answered in five minutes and did
# not need three weeks. Gate 2 still needs the analysis-in-a-separate-process
# work before 10 MSPS is deployable.
#
# Centred 462.8 rather than 466.0: at 2.5 MSPS the span is 461.55-464.05, which
# holds every FRS/GMRS output channel plus the whole periodic-emitter cluster
# this run is meant to identify — 461.675, 462.05, 462.30, 462.50, 463.50,
# 463.55, 463.90. It gives up the 467.x repeater inputs, which Phase 7 needs and
# this gate does not.
#
# Gain and ppm come from the profile: 42 and 0.64. Gain is 42 and not 39 because
# the antenna changed — see the profile.
#
# Audio capture on. 12000 events/hour at ~16 kB/s of traffic is roughly 2.3 GB
# a day, so 40 GB is about two and a half weeks; the budget stops capture and
# lets logging continue, so overrunning it costs audio, never events. Disk is
# 435 GB free. This is what lets the periodic emitters on 461-470 be identified
# offline instead of guessed at.
#
# Its own database, not data/survey.sqlite — that one holds the synthetic
# fixture scenario the test suite depends on.
RFSURVEY_DB=data/phase4.sqlite
RFSURVEY_ARGS=--freq 462.8e6 --rate 2.5e6 --capture-dir data/captures --capture-mb 40000
